{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And the people stood at a distance, and Moses drew near.</b> Now was it not already stated, ״וירא העם ויעמדו מרחוק״? But it is possible to explain that the first is distance of place — they distanced themselves further from the boundary that Moses had permitted them to stand within — whereas now it comes to hint at distance of apprehension, and to say that even though all Israel merited being prophets in the holy assembly when they heard the Ten Commandments from the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He, their apprehension cannot be compared to the apprehension of Moses; and the subject of the verse is to explain that the people's apprehension stood far from the place where Moses drew near. And the word ערפל, mentioned in Scripture, the commentators always explained to be darkness, in the manner of (Psalms 97:2) ״ענן וערפל סביביו״, and the meaning is that the Glory is hidden and concealed even from the ministering angels, and this is what is written (Psalms 18:12) ״ישת חשך סתרו סביבותיו סכתו״." "<b>And the correct interpretation</b> is that ערפל is a bright, clear light, and in the expression of the word ערפל — ערוי אפל, meaning that the darkness is plucked and absent from there; and this term is applied to the intensity of the great light. For just as darkness conceals a thing within it so that it is not seen, so the intensity of the mighty, strong light of the Countenance of Glory conceals and prevents the gazer from gazing upon it. And the proof that the word ערפל is light is what he mentioned here, ״אשר שם האלהים״, from what is written (Daniel 2:22) ״ונהורא עמיה שרא״, and this is what we say in prayer: ״ונגלית עליהם בערפלי טוהר״. Now Moses did not enter within the ערפל but drew near to it, like a person who draws near to the gate of the king but does not enter within the gate, and this is the language of ״ומשה נגש״ and so on. And Onkelos translated לצית אמיטתא — that is, to the very boundary of the reach that Moses reached; up to there and not beyond, and this is the meaning of ״אשר שם האלהים״. And then ״וידבר אלהים״ — and all Israel heard — and this is what He said to him first (Exodus 19:9): ״הנה אנכי בא אליך בעב הענן בעבור ישמע העם בדברי עמך״. And the subject of this passage, ״וכל העם רואים את הקולות״, was before the giving of the Torah, for thus the language proves; and ערפל — this is עב הענן that He mentioned regarding Moses: ״הנה אנכי בא אליך בעב הענן״; and likewise Israel, standing at the foot of the mountain, would see with their own eyes the appearance of the Glory like fire consuming the top of the mountain."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "Source cites תהלים צ׳׳ז; normalized to Psalms 97."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:48.733133458Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}